  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Developing Nigeria Circular Economy Program (NCEP) Roadmap Framework</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overarching goal of this project is to propose a plan for Nigeria to guide her transition from a linear and unsustainable economic model to a circular economy model. The proposed study will provide a roadmap framework (component 3) towards a Nigerian Circular Economy Program and complement the overall study of the African Development Bank (AfDB), which consists of the following three components:1)	Preparation of a Scoping Study on Circular Economy &amp; Green Growth.2)	Design of an MRV Framework for measuring, assessing, reporting, &amp; verifying circular economy &amp; natural capital within the Nigerian context to build back a better, greener and more resilient economy post-COVID-19.3)	Design of a Nigeria Circular Economy Program (NCEP) Roadmap Framework (2023 &#x2013; 2050).With this study, the AfDB, in collaboration with the Government of the Netherlands, aims to support the Federal Government of Nigeria&apos;s efforts at developing Circular Economy and natural capital accounting frameworks.</narrative>
  </description>
